# init.m95.modem.rc — Meizu MX6 (m95), MT6797 modem bring-up:
# md1 (GSM/WCDMA/LTE) + md3 (C2K/CDMA).
#
# The MX6 is full-netcom: ro.mtk_c2k_support=1, ro.mtk_enable_md3=1,
# ril.external.md=0, mtk.eccci.c2k=enabled [DEV: stock Flyme 8.0.5.0A
# system build.prop], and the md1img/md1dsp/md1arm7/md3img partitions exist
# on device [DEV: sepolicy file_contexts, scatter]. C2K runs over the
# integrated CCCI (eccci), not the legacy VIA SDIO path.
#
# SERVICE NAMES ARE LOAD-BEARING — the daemons chain-start each other via
# hardcoded ctl.start property values [FACT: strings on the m95 blobs]:
#   ccci_mdinit  -> "ccci_fsd", "gsm0710muxd", "gsm0710muxdmd2"
#   gsm0710muxd  -> "ril-daemon-mtk"
#   rc trigger   -> "ril-proxy" on ril.rilproxy=1 [DEV: stock init.rilproxy.rc:51]
# Do not rename services in this file.
#
# Socket layout follows stock's EFFECTIVE config: stock defines ril-daemon-mtk
# TWICE (init.modem.rc:67 with rild* sockets; init.rilproxy.rc:26 with mrild*
# sockets). init.rilproxy.rc is imported first (stock init.mt6797.rc:8 vs :20),
# so init rejected the init.modem.rc duplicate and the C2K/rilproxy layout —
# ril-proxy owns sockets rild..rild4, mtkrild owns mrild* — is what actually
# ran on this device. librilproxy.so contains rild/rild2/rild3/rild4 and
# librilmtk.so contains mrild/mrild2 [FACT: strings], consistent with that.
#
# RESOLVED 2026-08-09 (this comment previously called the framework<->RIL
# bridge an unsolved work item; that is no longer true). Pie telephony works
# through the HIDL path and the socket path is vestigial. Measured on the
# booted device [FACT, HANDOFF_NEXT_REVIEW.md §4.1]:
#   lshal          -> android.hardware.radio@1.0::IRadio/slot1 and /slot2
#                     registered by rild, with system_server as their client
#   gsm0710muxd    -> "Frames received/dropped: 430/0"
#   rild           -> "AT> AT+EFUN=1" / "AT< OK", "AT> AT+CPIN?"
#   /proc/net/unix -> every rild*/mrild* socket is state 01, no peer connected
# So RILJ never opens a unix socket here: it speaks IRadio to ril-daemon-mtk.

on post-fs-data
    # gsm0710muxd symlinks its pty slaves to /dev/radio/ptty* and mtk-ril
    # connects there; nobody else creates the directory. [DEV: stock
    # init.mt6797.rc:154 ("create for muxd pts device node"), same
    # post-fs-data trigger]
    mkdir /dev/radio 0770 radio radio

    # Modem NV + config dirs [DEV: stock init.modem.rc:21-43]
    mkdir /data/nvram/md 0770 root system
    mkdir /data/nvram/md3 0770 root system
    mkdir /data/md3 0770 root system
    mkdir /data/ccci_cfg 0770 system radio
    restorecon_recursive /data/ccci_cfg
    chown radio radio /sys/kernel/ccci/boot

##############################
# CCCI modem filesystem servers + modem-image loaders.
# Not disabled: auto-start with class core, as stock. ccci_mdinit also
# re-ctl.starts ccci_fsd on modem restart [FACT: strings].
##############################

# md1 [DEV: stock init.modem.rc:141-151]
service ccci_fsd /vendor/bin/ccci_fsd 0
    class core
    user radio
    group radio system
    oneshot

service ccci_mdinit /vendor/bin/ccci_mdinit 0
    class core
    user system
    group radio system
    oneshot

# md3 / C2K [DEV: stock init.modem.rc:153-163; md3img partition + eccci C2K
# props verified — see header]
service ccci3_fsd /vendor/bin/ccci_fsd 2
    class core
    user radio
    group radio system
    oneshot

service ccci3_mdinit /vendor/bin/ccci_mdinit 2
    class core
    user system
    group radio system
    oneshot

##############################
# 07.10 MUX daemons — started by ccci_mdinit via ctl.start [FACT: strings].
##############################

# [DEV: stock init.modem.rc:46-51]
service gsm0710muxd /vendor/bin/gsm0710muxd -s /dev/ttyC0 -f 512 -n 8 -m basic
    class core
    user root
    group radio cache inet misc
    disabled
    oneshot

# md2 does not exist on MT6797 (md1+md3 SoC), but ccci_mdinit carries a
# ctl.start reference to this name [FACT: strings]; kept disabled so a stray
# ctl.start hits a defined-but-disabled service instead of an init error.
# [DEV: stock init.modem.rc:53-58]
service gsm0710muxdmd2 /vendor/bin/gsm0710muxdmd2 -s /dev/ccci2_tty0 -f 512 -n 8 -m basic
    class core
    user root
    group radio cache inet misc
    disabled
    oneshot

##############################
# RIL daemons. mtkrild/mtkrildmd2 exec labels are rild_exec -> base rild
# domain (sepolicy decision, sepolicy/README.md).
##############################

# Started by gsm0710muxd via ctl.start once MUX channels are up. Disassembly
# of gsm0710muxd (FUN_000139a0, args resolved from the literal pools) proves
# the exact sequence on mux success: property_set("ctl.stop","ril-daemon")
# then property_set("ctl.start","ril-daemon-mtk"), then setuid(radio).
# "ril-daemon" is the AOSP Pie rild from rild.legacy.rc (class main) — the
# instance that on the 2026-08-07 boot loaded mtk-ril.so via rild.libpath and
# registered IRadio 1.1 [FACT: m95-logcat-1821.txt:6-13 +
# init.svc.ril-daemon=running live]. It is the ONLY Pie-framework-compatible
# RIL: the Nougat mtkrild registers unix sockets, no HIDL.
#
# So this service must be the AOSP rild binary, not mtkrild: muxd kills the
# HIDL rild and starts THIS name; pointing it at mtkrild would trade the
# working HIDL registration for a socket RIL Pie cannot talk to. Running
# rild here also fixes ordering: it now starts only after /dev/radio/ptty*
# exist instead of retrying every 10 s. (Previous exec:
# /vendor/bin/mtkrild — stock's Nougat layout, init.rilproxy.rc:26-48; the
# mrild* socket set is kept, mtk-ril.so grabs its control sockets from the
# environment.)
#
# Android 13: the library comes from `-l`, not from rild.libpath. On 18.1
# PRODUCT_COMPATIBLE_PROPERTY was false (measured, device-18.1 device.mk), so
# rild read rild.libpath/rild.libargs. On lineage-20 build/make/core/config.mk
# forces it true, rild is built with -DPRODUCT_COMPATIBLE_PROPERTY and reads
# vendor.rild.libpath/vendor.rild.libargs instead; with neither set it logged
# "RILd param count=1" and went straight to "RIL_Init starting sleep loop"
# without ever opening mtk-ril.so [FACT: meizu-fleet/captures/
# m95-boot-20260924-113630/logcat-1.txt:5486-5488].
#   - The path is NOT set as vendor.rild.libpath: vendor.ril-daemon below
#     (class main, disabled) is started anyway by every `class_restart main`
#     (vndservicemanager.rc onrestart; init's Service::Restart() starts a
#     stopped service regardless of `disabled`), and with that property it
#     would load a second mtk-ril.so next to this one.
#   - The args are NOT passed after `--`: in that branch rild appends
#     "-c <id>" through the argv array itself, i.e. over argv's NULL and
#     envp[0]. They come from vendor.rild.libargs (vendor.prop) instead,
#     which rild copies into a static array.
service ril-daemon-mtk /vendor/bin/hw/rild -l mtk-ril.so
    class core
    socket mrild stream 660 root radio
    socket mrild2 stream 660 root radio
    socket mrild3 stream 660 root radio
    socket mrild4 stream 660 root radio
    # No explicit seclabel here on purpose. Naming the label makes init
    # create the socket OBJECT with that type, which it may not do:
    #   avc: denied { create } scontext=u:r:init tcontext=rild_ims_socket
    #        tclass=unix_stream_socket
    # and the socket then does not exist at all. Declaring the socket here
    # is enough by itself: init creates the node and file_contexts labels
    # it, which is exactly how the neighbouring rild-oem gets its own type.
    # The label was missing before only because rild bound the socket
    # itself, with no declaration for init to act on.
    socket rild-ims stream 660 root radio
    socket rild-debug stream 660 radio system
    socket rild-oem stream 660 radio system
    socket rild-mtk-ut stream 660 radio net_bt
    socket rild-mtk-ut-2 stream 660 radio net_bt
    socket rild-mtk-modem stream 660 radio system
    socket rild-atci stream 660 root radio
    socket rild-mal stream 660 radio system
    socket rild-mal-at stream 660 radio system
    socket rild-vsim stream 660 root radio
    socket rild-mbim stream 660 root radio
    socket msap_uim_socket1 stream 660 radio radio
    socket msap_uim_socket2 stream 660 radio radio
    user root
    group radio cache inet misc audio sdcard_r sdcard_rw log system
    disabled
    # NO `oneshot` — deliberate divergence from stock (stock/m681-template
    # init.rilproxy.rc:52 marks mtkrild oneshot).
    #
    # Stock can afford oneshot because MTK's only expected rild death is a
    # modem exception, and ccci_mdinit re-issues ctl.start after it restarts
    # the MD [FACT: strings -a vendor/bin/ccci_mdinit -> "ctl.stop",
    # "ctl.start", "ril-daemon-mtk", "check_to_restart_md kill ril-proxy"].
    # Our rild dies for a *software* reason instead (see BLOB_SHIMS /
    # HANDOFF: mtk-ril.so calls s_rilenv->[+32] and ->[+40], which are past
    # the end of AOSP Pie's 32-byte struct RIL_Env, so it does `blr 0`
    # [FACT: tombstone_09 pc=0 at onUsimDetected+720; disassembly of
    # vendor/lib64/mtk-ril.so 0x92d34-0x92d38]). No MD exception happens, so
    # ccci_mdinit never restarts it.
    #
    # With `oneshot`, init's Reap() sets SVC_DISABLED and never restarts:
    # observed live 2026-08-09 after 12 h uptime — init.svc.ril-daemon-mtk
    # =stopped, no /dev/socket/mrild* (Reap unlinks them via
    # SocketInfo::Clean, system/core/init/descriptors.cpp:78), no IRadio in
    # lshal, 433 "RILJ: RadioProxy getService ... NoSuchElementException".
    # Telephony was unrecoverable for the whole session.
    #
    # AOSP's own rild.rc has no oneshot, and the copy of the SAME binary that
    # actually ships in /vendor/etc/init/rild.legacy.rc on this device is
    # `class main` with no oneshot either. Match that: a rild crash must be
    # survivable. NOTE: until the RIL_Env fix lands this turns one fatal
    # crash into a ~5 s restart loop — that is intentional and louder, not
    # quieter.

# [DEV: stock init.modem.rc:91-108] md2 RIL — same "defined but disabled"
# rationale as gsm0710muxdmd2. (Stock declares socket rild-vsim-md2 twice;
# deduplicated here.)
service ril-daemon-mtkmd2 /vendor/bin/mtkrildmd2
    class core
    socket rild-md2 stream 660 root radio
    socket rild2-md2 stream 660 root radio
    socket rild-debug-md2 stream 660 radio system
    socket rild-oem-md2 stream 660 radio system
    socket rild-mtk-ut-md2 stream 660 radio net_bt
    socket rild-mtk-ut-2-md2 stream 660 radio net_bt
    socket rild-mtk-modem-md2 stream 660 radio system
    socket rild-atci-md2 stream 660 root radio
    socket rild-vsim-md2 stream 660 root radio
    socket rild-mal-md2 stream 660 radio system
    socket rild-mbim-md2 stream 660 root radio
    user root
    group radio cache inet misc audio sdcard_r sdcard_rw log system
    disabled
    oneshot

# GSM<->C2K request router; owns the sockets the (Nougat) framework used.
# [DEV: stock init.rilproxy.rc:8-24, started via init.rilproxy.rc:50-51]
service ril-proxy /vendor/bin/rilproxy -l mtk-rilproxy.so
    class core
    socket rild stream 660 root radio
    socket rild2 stream 660 root radio
    socket rild3 stream 660 root radio
    socket rild4 stream 660 root radio
    socket rilproxy-atci stream 660 root radio
    socket rilproxy-mal stream 660 radio system
    socket sap_uim_socket1 stream 660 bluetooth bluetooth
    socket sap_uim_socket2 stream 660 bluetooth bluetooth
    socket sap_uim_socket3 stream 660 bluetooth bluetooth
    socket sap_uim_socket4 stream 660 bluetooth bluetooth
    socket embmsd stream 660 radio inet
    user root
    group radio cache inet misc audio sdcard_r sdcard_rw log system
    disabled
    oneshot

# NOT STARTED — deliberately. Stock's ril-proxy bridges the framework's unix
# sockets to mtkrild; our layout runs neither side of that bridge, so the
# daemon spends its whole life failing to connect to a peer that does not
# exist. Measured 2026-08-09 [FACT, HANDOFF_NEXT_REVIEW.md §4.4]:
#   logcat -b radio -> "connectSocket fail, try again -1" once a second,
#                      forever — ~3600 wasted log lines an hour
#   ps -A           -> only gsm0710muxd, rild and rilproxy exist; no mtkrild
#   /proc/net/unix  -> mrild/mrild2 have flags 00000000, i.e. never listened
#                      on, because mtkrild never ran to listen on them
#   /proc/net/unix  -> nothing is connected to rild/rild2/rild3/rild4 or
#                      sap_uim_socket*, the sockets ril-proxy itself owns
# Keeping the service *defined* (above) costs nothing and documents stock's
# layout; starting it only produces noise. The sockets it declares vanish
# with it, which is safe precisely because no peer ever connected to them.
#
# Re-enable this trigger if mtkrild is ever brought up, or if BT SIM Access
# Profile is needed — SAP is what sap_uim_socket* are for.
#
# on property:ril.rilproxy=1
#     start ril-proxy

# C2K RIL. With eccci C2K (ril.external.md=0) the SDIO tty argument is
# vestigial, but the cmdline is kept verbatim from stock. Library verified
# present: proprietary/vendor/lib/libviatelecom-withuim-ril.so [DEV: stock
# init.modem.rc:116-129].
service viarild /vendor/bin/viarild -l /vendor/lib/libviatelecom-withuim-ril.so -- -d /dev/ttySDIO4
    class core
    socket rild-via stream 660 radio radio
    socket msap_c2k_socket1 stream 660 radio radio
    socket msap_c2k_socket2 stream 660 radio radio
    socket msap_c2k_socket3 stream 660 radio radio
    socket msap_c2k_socket4 stream 660 radio radio
    socket rpc stream 660 radio system
    socket rild-ctclient stream 660 radio system
    socket rild-atci-c2k stream 660 radio system
    group radio cache inet misc audio sdcard_r sdcard_rw log system
    disabled
    oneshot

# NOTE: stock viarild also declares "socket rild-debug", colliding with
# ril-daemon-mtk's rild-debug (sockets are created at service start, so the
# later-started service would steal the node). Dropped here; the C2K debug
# path goes through rild-atci-c2k.

# Telephony Early Read — reads SIM/modem info early in boot.
# [DEV: stock init.modem.rc:192-196]
service terservice /vendor/bin/terservice
    class core
    user radio
    group radio cache inet misc
    oneshot

##############################
# AOSP rild neutralised.
##############################

# full_base_telephony.mk pulls in AOSP rild; its rc
# (hardware/ril/rild/rild.rc, parsed from /system/etc/init AFTER this
# ramdisk file, so THIS definition wins and the later duplicate is rejected)
# would run /vendor/bin/hw/rild as class main. With rild.libpath pointed at
# the Nougat mtk-ril.so that is a guaranteed crash-loop, and the socket RIL
# it served no longer exists in Pie. Defined here first and disabled.
# [FACT: telephony.mk:27 adds rild; rild.rc content verified in the Pie tree]
# lineage-20: `disabled` does not keep it down. Every vndservicemanager
# restart runs `class_restart main`, which starts it [FACT: 2026-09-24 11:36
# capture, started and SIGKILLed every ~5 s while vndservicemanager
# crash-looped]. It stays harmless only because it gets no library: no `-l`
# here and no vendor.rild.libpath anywhere, so rild takes its "no-ril" path.
service vendor.ril-daemon /vendor/bin/hw/rild
    class main
    user radio
    group radio cache inet misc audio log readproc wakelock
    disabled
    oneshot

##############################
# Modem loggers — all disabled; start manually (adb: start emdlogger1) when
# debugging radio bring-up. Domains mdlogger/emdlogger prepared in sepolicy.
##############################

# [DEV: stock init.mt6797.rc:1187-1227; emdlogger6 exists in stock rc but the
# binary is absent from our blob tree, so it is not defined]
service mdlogger /vendor/bin/mdlogger
    class main
    user shell
    group shell system radio sdcard_rw inet sdcard_r media_rw
    disabled
    oneshot

service emdlogger1 /vendor/bin/emdlogger1
    class main
    user shell
    group system shell radio sdcard_rw inet sdcard_r media_rw
    disabled
    oneshot

service emdlogger2 /vendor/bin/emdlogger2
    class main
    user shell
    group system shell radio sdcard_rw inet sdcard_r media_rw
    disabled
    oneshot

service emdlogger3 /vendor/bin/emdlogger3
    class main
    user shell
    group system shell radio sdcard_rw inet sdcard_r media_rw
    disabled
    oneshot

service emdlogger5 /vendor/bin/emdlogger5
    class main
    user shell
    group system shell radio sdcard_rw inet sdcard_r media_rw
    disabled
    oneshot
